  1200	# GH-141 — recoverability-only mitigation for the concurrent peer-edit race.
  1201	#
  1202	# rtl_check CANNOT distinguish "a peer session's concurrent mid-turn edit" from "the agent's own
  1203	# off-lane self-escape": both produce byte-identical porcelain diffs, and rtl_before's snapshot is
  1204	# taken once at turn start, so anything that turns dirty DURING the turn window looks identical.
  1205	# Any fix of the shape "don't revert a newly-dirty non-allowlisted path" would silently disable
  1206	# rtl_enforce's documented backstop against the already-observed GH-22 self-escape vector.
  1207	#
  1208	# So the revert DECISION IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED. This only copies the pre-revert content aside
  1209	# first, turning "not recoverable in general" (GH-141's live 2026-07-05 incident, and a second
  1210	# occurrence on 2026-07-18) into a recoverable one. Mirrors the refs/relay-orphan/<sha> pattern
  1211	# rtl_enforce already uses for the moved-HEAD case. Backups land under .tick/, which rtl_check
  1212	# exempts intrinsically, so a backup can never itself be flagged as off-lane.
