    25	. "$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/lib/fixture-guard.sh"
    26	fixture_guard_init "$WORK"
    27	trap 'rm -rf "$WORK"' EXIT
    28	
    29	PASS=0; FAIL=0
    30	pass() { echo "  PASS: $*"; PASS=$((PASS+1)); }
    31	fail() { echo "  FAIL: $*"; FAIL=$((FAIL+1)); }
    32	
    33	# A throwaway repo standing in for RTL_ROOT with one committed allowlist lane file.
    34	R="$WORK/repo"
    35	mkdir -p "$R"
    36	require_fixture "$R" "fixture repo"
    37	git -C "$R" init -q
    38	git -C "$R" config user.email t@example.com
    39	git -C "$R" config user.name t
    40	printf 'lane v1\n' >"$R/lane.md"
    41	git -C "$R" add -A
    42	git -C "$R" commit -qm init
    43	
    44	# shellcheck source=/dev/null
    45	source "$LIB"
    46	RTL_ROOT="$R"
    47	RTL_TOOL="test"
    48	RTL_LOG=""
    49	RTL_LOG_REL=""
    50	RTL_ARTIFACT=""
    51	
    52	# ── (1) rtl_check: scratch under ROOT is exempted AND discarded, and the turn does not fail ─────
    53	RTL_ALLOW=("lane.md")
    54	printf 'lane v2\n' >"$R/lane.md"                          # the legitimate lane edit
    55	mkdir -p "$R/.relay-scratch"
    56	printf '{"lens":2}\n' >"$R/.relay-scratch/out2.json"      # the probe output that killed the real turn
    57	printf '{"lens":3}\n' >"$R/.relay-scratch/out3.json"
    58	RTL_VIOLATION=0
    59	rtl_check ".relay-scratch/out2.json"
    60	[ "$RTL_VIOLATION" -eq 0 ] && pass "rtl_check: a scratch write is NOT a violation" \
    61	  || fail "rtl_check: scratch write flagged as violation"
    62	[ ! -d "$R/.relay-scratch" ] && pass "rtl_check: the scratch dir is DISCARDED from ROOT (not committed, not lingering)" \
    63	  || fail "rtl_check: scratch dir still present in ROOT after the check"
    64	cmp -s <(printf 'lane v2\n') "$R/lane.md" && pass "rtl_check: the legitimate lane edit is untouched" \
    65	  || fail "rtl_check: lane edit damaged by scratch handling"
    66	
    67	# The collapsed-dir form (git shows ".relay-scratch/" when the dir is wholly untracked) — same branch.
    68	mkdir -p "$R/.relay-scratch"; printf 'x\n' >"$R/.relay-scratch/probe.json"
    69	RTL_VIOLATION=0
    70	rtl_check ".relay-scratch/"
    71	[ "$RTL_VIOLATION" -eq 0 ] && [ ! -d "$R/.relay-scratch" ] \
    72	  && pass "rtl_check: the collapsed '.relay-scratch/' status form is exempted and discarded too" \
    73	  || fail "rtl_check: collapsed-dir form not handled"
    74	
    75	# ── (2) containment still BITES: scratch is a room, not an amnesty ───────────────────────────────
    76	printf 'stray\n' >"$R/stray.txt"
    77	RTL_VIOLATION=0
    78	rtl_check "stray.txt"
    79	[ "$RTL_VIOLATION" -eq 1 ] && pass "CONTROL: a stray file OUTSIDE .relay-scratch still violates (exit-6 path intact)" \
    80	  || fail "CONTROL: stray write not flagged — the exemption is an amnesty, not a room"
    81	[ ! -f "$R/stray.txt" ] && pass "CONTROL: the stray file is reverted as before" \
    82	  || fail "CONTROL: stray file survived"
    83	# A lookalike prefix must NOT ride the exemption.
    84	mkdir -p "$R/.relay-scratch2"; printf 'x\n' >"$R/.relay-scratch2/out.json"
    85	RTL_VIOLATION=0
    86	rtl_check ".relay-scratch2/out.json"
    87	[ "$RTL_VIOLATION" -eq 1 ] && pass "CONTROL: '.relay-scratch2' (lookalike prefix) is NOT exempt" \
    88	  || fail "CONTROL: lookalike prefix .relay-scratch2 slipped the exemption"
    89	
    90	# ── (3) worktree isolation: begin pre-creates the dir, end exempts it and never copies it back ──
    25	2026-10-17 and four on 2026-11-12. GH-184's guard (`test/gh184-no-tracked-scratch.sh`) keeps Forge
    26	itself from tracking scratch, but nothing protects host repos.
    27	
    28	Repro (no model call): a repo with a committed `.relay-scratch/pdf/tracked.json`; source the lib, set
    29	`RTL_ROOT`, call `rtl_check ".relay-scratch/pdf/tracked.json"` → `rc=0`, then `git status` shows
    30	` D .relay-scratch/pdf/tracked.json`.
    31	
    32	## Plan
    33	
    34	**Outcome.** Relay turns discard only the scratch a turn created (untracked or ignored files under
    35	`.relay-scratch/`); files the host repository tracks there are host content and get normal containment.
    36	
    37	**Smallest bet (two edits in `relay-turn-lib.sh`, nothing else):**
    38	1. `rtl_check`: the `.relay-scratch` exemption applies only when the path is not tracked
    39	   (`git -C "$RTL_ROOT" ls-files --error-unmatch -- "$p"` fails). A tracked path falls through to the
    40	   existing off-allowlist handling (orphan backup, `git checkout -- "$p"` restore, `RTL_VIOLATION=1`),
    41	   exactly as for any other host file. For the exempt case, replace `rm -rf` with
    42	   `git -C "$RTL_ROOT" clean -fdxq -- .relay-scratch` (removes untracked and ignored files and empty
    43	   untracked directories; leaves tracked files).
    44	2. `rtl_enforce` end-of-loop sweep: same `git clean -fdxq -- .relay-scratch` in place of `rm -rf`,
    45	   still unconditional and still independent of porcelain visibility (keeps the GH-91 / PR #93
    46	   ignored-scratch behaviour).
    47	
    48	**Not changed.** The worktree path (`rtl_worktree_end` `:898`, scratch never copied back) already cannot
    49	touch ROOT's tracked files. No change to prompts, GH-184's guard, or `.relay-artifacts`.
    50	
    51	**Not built.** No new test suite or `validate.sh` entry (GH-831). No host-side refusal or warning for
    52	tracked scratch.
    53	
    54	**Alternatives rejected.**
    55	- Refuse to run when a host tracks `.relay-scratch/`: blocks relays in repos that did nothing harmful.
    56	- Leave the code and tell hosts not to track there: the harness silently deletes data until someone reads the docs.
    57	
    58	**Rollback.** Revert the commit; behaviour returns to the blanket sweep. Easy.
    59	
    60	**Acceptance.**
    61	- The #1137 repro leaves `git status` clean and the tracked file present (red control: same repro on `edcb39a6e` shows ` D`).
    62	- Turn-created scratch still disappears, folder included: existing `test/gh91-relay-scratch.sh` (sections 1 and 6) passes unchanged.
    63	- A turn that modifies or deletes a tracked `.relay-scratch` file is reverted and flagged like any other off-lane edit (manual check).
    64	- Existing suites `gh91-relay-scratch.sh`, `gh113-headless-scratch.sh`, `gh184-no-tracked-scratch.sh`, `gh654-offlane-log.sh`; the routed tier-3 gate (`validate.sh`) once on the final commit in a disposable full clone.
    65	
    66	## Rating (2026-11-12)
    67	
    68	`rated 60/60/50/85` — sev 60: silently deletes tracked host files after every relay turn; recoverable
    69	with `git checkout`, but a `git add -A` after a turn commits the loss, and it recurs every turn;
    70	pri 60: operator asked for the fix now, recurring across lanes for a month; appeal 50: neutral, no
    71	operator score; effort 85: two lines plus manual verification. Recurrence: 8 deleting turns observed
    72	across two dates (2026-10-17, 2026-11-12) in one host repo; trend in other hosts unknown.

