e/issues/129", "raw_text": "- **#129/#130/#131 · Wave 1 of the Harness Driver & Relay Seam Hardening marathon — three preflighted driver/relay fixes** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-22 (PR #134, squash d92236cb; issues closed)** — relay-drive self-resolves TICK_REPO_ROOT via resolve_turn_root when unset and replaces the misleading \"token missing\" with a diagnostic naming the resolved root and searched event dir, every escalation pinned at exit 4; the agy auth preflight classifies usage/CLI-syntax errors as unverifiable (non-blocking) while credentials errors stay exit 5; marathon-drive's phase write-set (RELAY.md/ESCALATION.md) commits route to `phase_commit_root` — the repo containing phase_dir — making `--target-root` + target `--phases-dir` runnable for the first time. Three suites (33 assertions) with recorded pre-fix negative controls; full gate 233/233; first-gate run caught the gh376 twin-parity ordering defect (NOTE must print after the lock refusal). Follow-ups filed as #135-#140. → [#129](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/129) · [#130](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/130) · [#131](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/131) (rated 72/60/65/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 72, "rating_sev": 60, "rating_appeal": 65, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0H9CC0981F9CSAMV7BXRYXP", "gh_number": 111, "title": "GH-111 · retire manifest FREEZE; tasks and marathons are DIALED IN to exactly one release, as a database state", "section": "Completed", "position": 35, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-111-DIALED-IN.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/111", "raw_text": "- **GH-111 · retire manifest FREEZE; tasks and marathons are DIALED IN to exactly one release, as a database state** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-21 (PR #116; issue closed)** — membership became machine-checkable instead of a sentence someone remembered to write: three states (`dialed_in`/`shipped`/`cut`), exclusivity by a partial unique index over ACTIVE membership only, a real `releases migrate` upgrade path where none existed, and BASELINES replacing what the freeze used to buy (progress against the live manifest, growth against the kickoff count). Closed #109 (the viewer asserted marathon membership the data never claimed) and #110 (`shipped` was a state nothing could write). rated 85/75/70/35. → [GH-111-DIALED-IN.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-111-DIALED-IN.md) · [#111](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/111)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 85, "rating_sev": 75, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 35, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3B6RQB0PQJK017M2RCHE2", "gh_number": 410, "title": "relay-block validator never runs on the driven path", "section": "Completed", "position": 35, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-410-RELAY-BLOCK-VALIDATOR-DRIVEN-PATH.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/410", "raw_text": "- **GH-410 · The structural relay-block validator never runs on the driven path, and rejects the bold STATUS format real threads write** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #434)** — §12's separated-grading guarantee is enforced only when the model volunteers --relay-file. Plus two follow-on defects: the rtl_enforce backstop no-ops on the healthy path (GH-67), and the validator's literal ^STATUS: match rejects the bold form real threads write (GH-92). Zero test coverage today. /3/3/3 [ovr 4] — [GH-410-RELAY-BLOCK-VALIDATOR-DRIVEN-PATH.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-410-RELAY-BLOCK-VALIDATOR-DRIVEN-PATH.md) · [#410](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/410) (rated 95/80/90/40)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 95, "rating_sev": 80, "rating_appeal": 90, "rating_effort": 40, "rating_ovr": 4, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0H9CC0AAF9JWBSHR3679NQQ", "gh_number": 108, "title": "GH-108 · pri/sev/appeal/effort — the canonical task rating system (calc sum + operator override)", "section": "Completed", "position": 36, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-108-RATING-SYSTEM.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/108", "raw_text": "- **GH-108 · pri/sev/appeal/effort — the canonical task rating system (calc sum + operator override)** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-21 (PR #116; issue closed)** — one scoring vocabulary for every task in the ledger, oriented so a single glance answers what should go to the front of the line: four axes 1-100 where higher is always better (effort scores cheapness), a combined 4-400 `calc` derived and never stored, and an `ovr` override that pins anything visible. Authored as `rated N/N/N/N` on a ROADMAP entry; read via `bash utils/leaderboard.sh` or LEADERBOARD.html. rated 80/50/75/40. → [GH-108-RATING-SYSTEM.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-108-RATING-SYSTEM.md) · [#108](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/108)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 80, "rating_sev": 50, "rating_appeal": 75, "rating_effort": 40, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3B78KQ2A649QHFWXF9VJE", "gh_number": 412, "title": "transient claim collision indistinguishable from durable loss", "section": "Completed", "position": 36, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-412-TRANSIENT-CLAIM-EXIT-CODE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/412", "raw_text": "- **GH-412 · A transient O_EXCL claim collision exits 1, identical to a durable loss — no retry channel under marathon load** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #431)** — no retry channel under marathon load** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #431)** — no retry channel under marathon load** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — lock.js throws a bare Error on EEXIST, tick maps every throw to 1, rtl.py fails the turn with no retry. Follow-up to shipped GH-408, which unified the three DURABLE lost exits and never considered EEXIST. Distinct exit 75 plus a --json result line. /3/3/2 [ovr 4] — [GH-412-TRANSIENT-CLAIM-EXIT-CODE.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-412-TRANSIENT-CLAIM-EXIT-CODE.md) · [#412](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/412) (rated 80/75/75/55)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 80, "rating_sev": 75, "rating_appeal": 75, "rating_effort": 55, "rating_ovr": 4, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0H9CC0A81K3083ASEGK37HK", "gh_number": null, "title": "Execution checklist for GH-111 + GH-108", "section": "Completed", "position": 37, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-108-GH-111-EXECUTION-TODO.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/111", "raw_text": "- **Execution checklist for GH-111 + GH-108** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-21 (PR #116)** — the running list covering every deliverable of the two plans above, in dependency order, so a stall at any point left the next move unambiguous. Retired with them: both plans are now in 3-COMPLETED, which was this doc's own stated end condition. rated 40/20/35/95. → [GH-108-GH-111-EXECUTION-TODO.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-108-GH-111-EXECUTION-TODO.md) · [#111](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/111)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 40, "rating_sev": 20, "rating_appeal": 35, "rating_effort": 95, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3B7MK4Y0S1T8B9Z6PANAJ", "gh_number": 413, "title": "launch-artifact marker authorises destructive rebuild", "section": "Completed", "position": 37, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-413-LAUNCH-ARTIFACT-MARKER-DESTRUCTION.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/413", "raw_text": "- **GH-413 · The launch-artifact marker authorises a destructive rebuild of any directory — marker alone, no git history required** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #426)** — marker alone, no git history required** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #426)** — marker alone, no git history required** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — E1 at HEAD: a dir holding nothing but a copied marker and two files passes the destination guard; the control without the marker is refused. Both halves (marker plus build script) are tracked, so any public reader holds the mechanism. Delete the marker; guard multi-commit destinations. /4/1/1 [ovr 4] — [GH-413-LAUNCH-ARTIFACT-MARKER-DESTRUCTION.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-413-LAUNCH-ARTIFACT-MARKER-DESTRUCTION.md) · [#413](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/413) (rated 90/95/85/95)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 90, "rating_sev": 95, "rating_appeal": 85, "rating_effort": 95, "rating_ovr": 4, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0FY5VR7R33M0WVBBCNJSTA3", "gh_number": 101, "title": "GH-101 · Feasibility Study: Promoting Programmatic Script Runner (`script_runner.py`) into Core Relay & Consult Runtimes", "section": "Completed", "position": 38, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-101-FEASIBILITY-STUDY-SCRIPT-RUNNER.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/101", "raw_text": "- **GH-101 · Feasibility Study: Promoting Programmatic Script Runner (`script_runner.py`) into Core Relay & Consult Runtimes** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-20 (issue closed)** — evaluated and promoted programmatic tool mode across `consult.py` and `relay_drive.py` behind `--tool-mode programmatic` (default off); completed 3-test qualification ladder (Test 1 architectural review & fail-closed threat scoping; Test 2 consult dogfooding with throwaway worktree isolation, pre-created `.relay-scratch/`, and 1,935-trial paired density benchmark in `TESTS-RESULTS/2026-08-20+GH-101/`; Test 3 relay-drive PGID process cleanup stress and fail-closed sandbox checks in `test/synthetic/gh101-relay-programmatic-stress.sh`); promoted to Production-Ready (A-Grade) in `HARNESS-MODELS-REGISTRY.md`. → [GH-101-FEASIBILITY-STUDY-SCRIPT-RUNNER.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-101-FEASIBILITY-STUDY-SCRIPT-RUNNER.md) · [#101](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/101) (rated 45/20/70/40)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 45, "rating_sev": 20, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 40, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3CA27TY8RHZ7KQMXXCC5Y", "gh_number": 411, "title": "tick log exempt from the foreign-cwd guard", "section": "Completed", "position": 38, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-411-TICK-LOG-FOREIGN-CWD-GUARD.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/411", "raw_text": "- **GH-411 · tick log is exempt from the foreign-cwd guard — the verb that seeds every run, plus the whole marathon namespace** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-03 (PR #420)** — the verb that seeds every run, plus the whole marathon namespace** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — assertResolvedRoot returns early on the verb not the event type, so task.created and every marathon type seed a .tick log in whatever cwd resolved. Guard everything except cost. — [GH-411-TICK-LOG-FOREIGN-CWD-GUARD.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-411-TICK-LOG-FOREIGN-CWD-GUARD.md) · [#411](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/411) (rated 75/70/70/80)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 75, "rating_sev": 70, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 80, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0GKR98K9X9FYJVH6CPSQ2BP", "gh_number": 103, "title": "GH-103 · technical spike: RELEASES SQLite → timeline-ui ledger viewer (RELEASES dashboard view)", "section": "Completed", "position": 39, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-103-TIMELINE-LEDGER-SPIKE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/103", "raw_text": "- **GH-103 · technical spike: RELEASES SQLite → timeline-ui ledger viewer (RELEASES dashboard view)** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-20 (PR #104)** — read-only exporter `utils/timeline/export_timeline.py` projects `releases.db` into timeline-ui's `data.json` contract; viewer `utils/timeline/RELEASES.html` (header collapse caret, full-viewport liquid layout, scrollable detour lanes); `--preview` bakes the committed `RELEASES-PREVIEW.html` snapshot, auto-refreshed after every CLI write by the GH-106 hook; `--serve` answers `/data.json` live from the DB; band-aware RELEASES.md-vs-DB drift banner. Zero DB writes (SQLite `mode=ro`). Prototype for the queued #75 `releases dashboard` verb; follow-on integration tracked in #107 (Cargo). → [GH-103-TIMELINE-LEDGER-SPIKE.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-103-TIMELINE-LEDGER-SPIKE.md) · [#103](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/103) (rated 62/35/75/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 62, "rating_sev": 35, "rating_appeal": 75, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3CAEDR1GFMEPRDEQ1T924", "gh_number": 414, "title": "nothing checks whether an inline code comment is still true", "section": "Completed", "position": 39, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-414-COMMENT-REFERENCE-CHECK.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/414", "raw_text": "- **GH-414 · Nothing deterministic checks whether an inline code comment is still true — extend the dead-reference resolver past the doc boundary** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #427)** — extend the dead-reference resolver past the doc boundary** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #427)** — extend the dead-reference resolver past the doc boundary** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #427)** — extend the dead-reference resolver past the doc boundary** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — pdda-check-governance already resolves dead references in markdown; it stops at the document boundary, so kernel comments citing absent ADRs stay green forever. Extend the glob to source comments, run against both trees, and triage the existing warning stream. — [GH-414-COMMENT-REFERENCE-CHECK.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-414-COMMENT-REFERENCE-CHECK.md) · [#414](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/414) (rated 60/45/85/70)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 60, "rating_sev": 45, "rating_appeal": 85, "rating_effort": 70, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0G0PGX85DBNMZC2HSJ6MF7H", "gh_number": 102, "title": "GH-102 · Unify Telemetry Schema & Inspection Tooling Across Fuzzing and ATE", "section": "Completed", "position": 40, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-102-UNIFIED-TELEMETRY-TOOLING.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/102", "raw_text": "- **GH-102 · Unify Telemetry Schema & Inspection Tooling Across Fuzzing and ATE** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-20 (issue closed)** — standardized shared data contract (`schema_version: \"1.0\"`), instrumented `utils/fuzzing/fuzz-loop.sh` with argv-safe JSONL emission and sub-second millisecond timing; updated `utils/ate/scripts/run_variations.py` to triage `tokens_source` (`api_usage` vs `config_provided` vs `unsupported`); upgraded `utils/ate/scripts/checkin.py` into a universal inspector with nearest-rank percentiles and comparative side-by-side mode; verified via `test/synthetic/gh102-telemetry-schema.sh` (8/8 PASS) and archived receipts in `TESTS-RESULTS/2026-08-20+GH-102/`. → [GH-102-UNIFIED-TELEMETRY-TOOLING.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-102-UNIFIED-TELEMETRY-TOOLING.md) · [#102](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/102) (rated 68/45/70/45)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 68, "rating_sev": 45, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 45, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3CATFWYEBT1934NQW6J9E", "gh_number": 415, "title": "guard hook covers 6 of 12 Tier-A entrypoints", "section": "Completed", "position": 40, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-415-GUARD-HOOK-DERIVE-ENTRYPOINTS.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/415", "raw_text": "- **GH-415 · The skill-first guard hook covers 6 of 12 Tier-A entrypoints — derive the set from AGENTS.md instead of hardcoding it** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #438)** — derive the set from AGENTS.md instead of hardcoding it** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #438)** — derive the set from AGENTS.md instead of hardcoding it** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-09-04 (PR #438)** — derive the set from AGENTS.md instead of hardcoding it** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — six literal filenames against a surface of twelve; the authoritative enumeration already exists at AGENTS.md 230-232. Direct instance of Radar T3's open derive-from-source item. Also fixes a false positive where any command merely mentioning a driver path is blocked. — [GH-415-GUARD-HOOK-DERIVE-ENTRYPOINTS.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-415-GUARD-HOOK-DERIVE-ENTRYPOINTS.md) · [#415](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/415) (rated 65/55/70/80)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 65, "rating_sev": 55, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 80, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0EWSZJX1WYGDFBNMS2TJFT0", "gh_number": 94, "title": "GH-94 · research: programmatic tool calling & code-mode execution for harnesses, telemetry, and containment", "section": "Completed", "position": 41, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-94-PROGRAMMATIC-TOOL-CALLING.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/94", "raw_text": "- **GH-94 · research: programmatic tool calling & code-mode execution for harnesses, telemetry, and containment** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-20 (PR #100; issue closed)** — implemented `utils/py/script_runner.py` with AST serialization normalization, PGID process-group session management (`setsid`), and fail-closed macOS seatbelt sandboxing (`sandbox-exec`); instrumented `utils/ate/scripts/run_variations.py` with telemetry schema 1.0; completed 438-iteration variation campaign with local Gemma 4 classifier triage archived in `TESTS-RESULTS/2026-08-20+GH-94/`; verified synthetic suites `gh94-script-serialization.sh` and `gh94-containment-invariants.sh` (7/7 PASS). → [GH-94-PROGRAMMATIC-TOOL-CALLING.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-94-PROGRAMMATIC-TOOL-CALLING.md) · [#94](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/94) (rated 45/20/70/40)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 45, "rating_sev": 20, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 40, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DP23V80KAQSQP9C3V07BS0", "gh_number": 57, "title": "GH-57 · test(releases): SQLite ledger fuzzing recipes & multi-scenario resilience suite", "section": "Completed", "position": 42, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-57-RELEASES-SQLITE-FUZZING.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/57", "raw_text": "- **GH-57 · test(releases): SQLite ledger fuzzing recipes & multi-scenario resilience suite** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-19 (PR #60 + PR #70; issue closed)** — synthetic fuzzing recipes and edge-case scenario coverage in `test/gh57-releases-fuzz.sh` (42/42 assertions) for concurrent branch divergence, multi-generation merge headers, duplicate settings/GID collisions, crash injection & journal recovery at 5 boundaries, common-dir lock contention, torn dump protection, and Markdown drift; evaluated non-interactive model routing across Muse Spark, Qwen 3.8-Max, GLM-5.2, and Codex. → [GH-57-RELEASES-SQLITE-FUZZING.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-57-RELEASES-SQLITE-FUZZING.md) · [#57](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/57) (rated 60/45/65/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 60, "rating_sev": 45, "rating_appeal": 65, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DP23V9XAQT9ZC2C2P7Y6MT", "gh_number": 45, "title": "GH-45 · validate.sh must refuse to run from a linked worktree — an observed run corrupted the parent clone", "section": "Completed", "position": 43, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-45-WORKTREE-GATE-REFUSAL.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/45", "raw_text": "- **GH-45 · validate.sh must refuse to run from a linked worktree — an observed run corrupted the parent clone** ✅ **SHIPPED 2026-08-18 (PR #55, built on `development` in clone `XYZ-forge-gh35`; issue closed 2026-08-19)** — `validate.sh` AND `ci-local.sh` now refuse (exit 2, before anything runs, every tier) when invoked from a linked git worktree, using the issue's verified `--absolute-git-dir` vs `--git-common-dir` comparison anchored on both HERE and the CWD. The refusal names the observed 2026-08-19 damage (core.bare=true, origin repointed, remote refs deleted, development overwritten with fixture commits); `XYZ_ALLOW_WORKTREE_GATE=1` overrides and announces itself. Pinned in `test/gh35-test-tiers.sh` §9 incl. the required control (normal checkout of the same repo still runs, silently). → [GH-45-WORKTREE-GATE-REFUSAL.md](PROJECT/3-COMPLETED/GH-45-WORKTREE-GATE-REFUSAL.md) · [#45](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/45) · [#564](https://github.com/Claude-AI-Tools-Ventura-County/xyz-3-agents-swarm/issues/564) (rated 65/60/60/70)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 65, "rating_sev": 60, "rating_appeal": 60, "rating_effort": 70, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1MAQ6G07ACPBGQY822RG1T9", "gh_number": 419, "title": "make the three marathon process rules deterministic", "section": "Completed", "position": 43, "status_marker": "✅", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-419-MARATHON-RULE-ENFORCEMENT.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/419", "raw_text": "- **GH-419 · Make the three marathon process rules deterministic — umbrella issue, full clone, derived clone name — by extending marathon.sh's existing --plan refusal** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — 