tional continuation held · [plan](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-1006-BOUNDED-RECOVERY.md) · [#1006](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/1006) (rated 80/65/80/45)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 80, "rating_sev": 65, "rating_appeal": 80, "rating_effort": 45, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0V4GQBGZE7TZCY3M4AB3CTZ", "gh_number": 223, "title": "GH-223 — pre-push gate push double-applies through ref lock", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 1, "status_marker": null, "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-223-GATE-PUSH-DOUBLE-APPLY.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/223", "raw_text": "- **GH-223 — pre-push gate push double-applies through ref lock** (2026-08-24) - gate-green push reports its own landed commit as a lock rejection; observed 2x of ~10 gated pushes; quick-fix shape. Captured via /idea; dialed into 0.9.0 Cargo. Issue [#223](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/223). -> [PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-223-GATE-PUSH-DOUBLE-APPLY.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-223-GATE-PUSH-DOUBLE-APPLY.md) (rated 80/75/65/60)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 80, "rating_sev": 75, "rating_appeal": 65, "rating_effort": 60, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0V0JQD8T7VH32KB1ZX97PD3", "gh_number": 215, "title": "GH-215 — wave_reconcile.py and roadmap-dashboard.sh hardcode pre-vendoring path depth", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 4, "status_marker": null, "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-215-RECONCILER-VENDOR-PATHS.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/215", "raw_text": "- **GH-215 — wave_reconcile.py and roadmap-dashboard.sh hardcode pre-vendoring path depth** (2026-08-24) - both assume a bare `utils/` at repo root; under vendored `.xyz/` they die on missing files / ENOENT. Fixed locally in the reporting repo, not yet upstream. Bug filed via /file-xyz-bug from `LTVera-Pandas`. Issue [#215](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/215). -> [PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-215-RECONCILER-VENDOR-PATHS.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-215-RECONCILER-VENDOR-PATHS.md) (rated 72/60/65/60)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 72, "rating_sev": 60, "rating_appeal": 65, "rating_effort": 60, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0V0JQD8MQPVYZ6KBTD1A1C9", "gh_number": 216, "title": "GH-216 — marathon-plan.sh ledger parser rejects link-style ROADMAP.md bullets", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 5, "status_marker": null, "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-216-LEDGER-BULLET-FORMAT.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/216", "raw_text": "- **GH-216 — marathon-plan.sh ledger parser rejects link-style ROADMAP.md bullets** (2026-08-24) - reconciler never completes in a repo whose ROADMAP.md uses `- [Title](path) — ...` bullets; exit 3 every time. Open design question, not patched. Bug filed via /file-xyz-bug from `LTVera-Pandas`. Issue [#216](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/216). -> [PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-216-LEDGER-BULLET-FORMAT.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-216-LEDGER-BULLET-FORMAT.md) (rated 75/65/70/70)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 75, "rating_sev": 65, "rating_appeal": 70, "rating_effort": 70, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DZZGNQVK65X0Y63AYGCM4E", "gh_number": 75, "title": "GH-75 · single-page HTML dashboard: releases (mid/long term) + roadmap (immediate) in one read-only view", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 7, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-75-RELEASES-ROADMAP-DASHBOARD.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/75", "raw_text": "- **GH-75 · single-page HTML dashboard: releases (mid/long term) + roadmap (immediate) in one read-only view** 🆕 **queued 2026-08-19 at the FRONT of the line (operator call)** — a `releases dashboard` verb renders one self-contained HTML file from `releases.db`, with a card per release (version, codename, status, target, days-to-target, manifest open/closed split, exit criterion) and a card per `roadmap_items` row grouped by section in ledger order, plus a header strip carrying generation, receipt count, and a stale-sync banner when `ROADMAP.md` is ahead of the shadow. Read-only by construction: no writer lock, no generation bump, no receipt — safe to run mid-merge. First real consumer of the GH-69 shadow rows. rated 90/40/85/55. → [#75](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/75)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 90, "rating_sev": 40, "rating_appeal": 85, "rating_effort": 55, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DZZGNRVEH9GPW7J3VPBP4B", "gh_number": 61, "title": "GH-61 · RELEASES ledger durability hardening (GH-57 follow-up)", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 8, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": null, "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/61", "raw_text": "- **GH-61 · RELEASES ledger durability hardening (GH-57 follow-up)** 🆕 **queued 2026-08-19 — filed 2026-08-19 out of the PR #60 review and un-triaged until now** — four scoped test follow-ups under one parent: exact ledger state asserted after crash recovery ([#62](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/62)), writer-lock stress and owner-death recovery ([#63](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/63)), seeded malformed-dump property coverage ([#64](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/64)), and a portable artifact-hash helper ([#65](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/65)). rated 45/55/40/50. → [#61](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/61)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 45, "rating_sev": 55, "rating_appeal": 40, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DQ00PCDP50DH1TFMSE4AV4", "gh_number": 67, "title": "GH-67 · Commandcode builder default widened to `--yolo` — closer evaluation → possible build", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 9, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": null, "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/67", "raw_text": "- **GH-67 · Commandcode builder default widened to `--yolo` — closer evaluation → possible build** 🆕 **queued 2026-08-19 as the NEXT immediate item (operator call, session close)** — PR #60 moved the default from the bounded `--permission-mode auto-accept` to `--yolo` (alias for `--dangerously-skip-permissions`), unmentioned in a fuzzing PR. Evaluate whether the turn shim’s containment (worktree isolation, `ALLOW_PATHS`, commit-bypass guard) genuinely makes the child CLI’s permission mode irrelevant; if yes, RATIFY — write the containment argument down in AGENTS.md/the shim docs and pin it — if no, revert the default and drop the `--yolo` test pin. Sibling check either way: `claude-turn.py` uses `--permission-mode acceptEdits`; confirm the two adapters differ on purpose. rated 88/80/45/70 ovr 340. → [#67](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/67)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 88, "rating_sev": 80, "rating_appeal": 45, "rating_effort": 70, "rating_ovr": 340, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DP23VAR6KPD0ZX6Q8WKWZR", "gh_number": 32, "title": "GH-32 · RELEASES app: SQLite-backed release ledger, CLI-only writes, generated RELEASES.md, cross-repo UI", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 10, "status_marker": "🚧", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-32-RELEASES-APP-SQLITE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/32", "raw_text": "- **GH-32 · RELEASES app: SQLite-backed release ledger, CLI-only writes, generated RELEASES.md, cross-repo UI** 🚧 **Phase 0+1 BUILT and merged 2026-08-19 (PR #34, builder GLM 5.3 per the #33 evaluation)** — schema/CLI/writer-protocol/canonical-dump/import landed (`utils/py/releases_app.py`, suite 81/0, full gate green, independently verified); the PRD survived a 4-round Codex sol-high relay review first. Still ahead: the `/releases` route migration (Phase 0 entry gate for the measured dogfood window), the Phase 2 strict flip, and the Phase 3 cockpit card. rated 70/50/65/35. → [GH-32-RELEASES-APP-SQLITE.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-32-RELEASES-APP-SQLITE.md) · [#32](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/32) · [#33](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/33)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 70, "rating_sev": 50, "rating_appeal": 65, "rating_effort": 35, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M0DP23VACJP47XMYQQ7E37RK", "gh_number": 28, "title": "GH-28 · RELEASES.md ledger discipline: deterministic bloat checks + per-release tracking issue", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 11, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-28-RELEASES-LEDGER-DISCIPLINE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/28", "raw_text": "- **GH-28 · RELEASES.md ledger discipline: deterministic bloat checks + per-release tracking issue** 🆕 **queued 2026-08-18, sharpened via /consult (single-model, agy quota-failed) 2026-08-18, post-Ballast 0.7.0 follow-up** — root cause is two gaps: the discipline rubric only fires on manual `/releases clean`, and release-level notes have no home of their own. Consult caught that the original plan would've reversed documented \"never blocks\" policy and that the parser can't see continuation-paragraph bloat at all — both fixed: checks are now permanently advisory, scoped to active/unshipped blocks, with a required parser-folding step. rated 40/35/40/55. → [GH-28-RELEASES-LEDGER-DISCIPLINE.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-28-RELEASES-LEDGER-DISCIPLINE.md) · [#28](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/28)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 40, "rating_sev": 35, "rating_appeal": 40, "rating_effort": 55, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id"