ON.md) · [#341](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/341) (rated 50/50/50/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 50, "rating_sev": 50, "rating_appeal": 50, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1HHWT3KSEJ9FJG2PWQ0A16K", "gh_number": 384, "title": "Explore a secure cross-device AgentChorus bridge over Cloudflare Tunnel", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 32, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-384-AGENTCHORUS-CLOUDFLARE-BRIDGE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/384", "raw_text": "- **GH-384 · Explore a secure cross-device AgentChorus bridge over Cloudflare Tunnel** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-01 via HQ** — [GH-384-AGENTCHORUS-CLOUDFLARE-BRIDGE.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-384-AGENTCHORUS-CLOUDFLARE-BRIDGE.md) · [#384](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/384) (rated 50/50/50/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 50, "rating_sev": 50, "rating_appeal": 50, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1JCNG85M66KMW9TECVE0EK1", "gh_number": 396, "title": "Harness root resolution: one resolver, two roots, pinned — retire RADAR-class-vendored-root-resolution", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 33, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-396-HARNESS-ROOT-RESOLVER.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/396", "raw_text": "- **GH-396 · Harness root resolution: one resolver, two roots, pinned** — retire RADAR-class-vendored-root-resolution (rated 50/50/50/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 50, "rating_sev": 50, "rating_appeal": 50, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1JM8DRGEBEE1CZ76N3BTN42", "gh_number": 399, "title": "Let the profile carry the route", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 33, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-399-PROFILE-CARRIES-THE-ROUTE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/399", "raw_text": "- **GH-399 — let the profile carry the route** (2026-09-02) - adding a model route means editing Python in three places; the device-config profile can only name a provider a shim already hardcodes, so an unknown one resolved cleanly and routed elsewhere. Two phases: the resolver emits base_url/key_env, the DeepSeek shim consumes them. rated 2/3/2/2. Issue [#399](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/399). -> [PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-399-PROFILE-CARRIES-THE-ROUTE.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-399-PROFILE-CARRIES-THE-ROUTE.md)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 2, "rating_sev": 3, "rating_appeal": 2, "rating_effort": 2, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1JSQJBARH07KNFSKNC1GQFR", "gh_number": 402, "title": "Board sync: auto-add issues to the Projects board when any agent starts work", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 34, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-402-BOARD-SYNC.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/402", "raw_text": "- **GH-402 · Board sync: auto-add issues to the Projects board when any agent starts work** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-02 via HQ** — [GH-402-BOARD-SYNC.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-402-BOARD-SYNC.md) · [#402](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/402) (rated 50/50/50/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 50, "rating_sev": 50, "rating_appeal": 50, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M0BT84BCG7MZTZXPSJKNYV", "gh_number": 406, "title": "External review (Russ K.): eight findings on guards that cover a narrower path than the doc claims", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 34, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-406-RUSS-EXTERNAL-REVIEW.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/406", "raw_text": "- **GH-406 · External review (Russ K.): eight findings on guards that cover a narrower path than the doc claims** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — all eight reproduce at HEAD; five are one class (a doc states a guarantee, the mechanism covers a narrower path, nothing compares the two — the §13 anti-pattern). R1 wire --relay-file into rtl_enforce · R2 guard tick log for task.* · R3 typed transient claim exit 75 · R4 drop the destructive-rebuild marker · R5 PDDA comment-reference check · R6 glob the guard hook. rated 3/3/4/3 [ovr 4] — [GH-406-RUSS-EXTERNAL-REVIEW.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-406-RUSS-EXTERNAL-REVIEW.md) · [#406](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/406)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 3, "rating_sev": 3, "rating_appeal": 4, "rating_effort": 3, "rating_ovr": 4, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M3CB6E0MKZNSCR4BM0EESS", "gh_number": 416, "title": "four documentation trues-ups", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 41, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-416-DOC-TRUES-UP-BATCH.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/416", "raw_text": "- **GH-416 · Four documentation trues-ups — package.json vs §7, dead PROJECT 4-MISC refs, CODEX_FLAGS default and dead escalation rung, uncommitted ROUTER pointer** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — each is a document stating something not literally true of the tree. CODEX_FLAGS has two halves: the default omits the approval flag AND the documented escalation rung is a no-op because that flag is already the default. — [GH-416-DOC-TRUES-UP-BATCH.md](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-416-DOC-TRUES-UP-BATCH.md) · [#416](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/416) (rated 50/30/60/95)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 50, "rating_sev": 30, "rating_appeal": 60, "rating_effort": 95, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1M9HWTHDERQGFZMFX3EQS60", "gh_number": 418, "title": "Marathon planner still reads the frozen ROADMAP.md", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 42, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-418-MARATHON-ADOPT-RELEASES-DB.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/418", "raw_text": "- **GH-418 · Marathon planner still reads the frozen ROADMAP.md — DB-parked items are invisible since the ROADMAP_SOURCE=releases flip** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-03 via HQ** — .pdda-mode says the DB is planning truth and router_audit calls ROADMAP.md frozen legacy, but marathon_plan.py:126 reads ROADMAP.md and neither planner file mentions the flip (0 grep hits). Proof: the 09-01/09-02 plans surface #349/#351, which exist only in ROADMAP.md and not in roadmap_items. 37 DB-parked items are unplannable. Concrete testable slice of GH-269. — [GH-418-MARATHON-ADOPT-RELEASES-DB.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-418-MARATHON-ADOPT-RELEASES-DB.md) · [#418](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/418) (rated 88/78/80/75) — depends on GH-423 (the rendered ledger artifact this planner consumes)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 88, "rating_sev": 78, "rating_appeal": 80, "rating_effort": 75, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1N0AXTVP8VJ9EPW8CJK1VNY", "gh_number": 421, "title": "Wave reconciliation is never invoked automatically — wire it post-merge, but fix its ledger write first", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 44, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-421-AUTO-WAVE-RECONCILE.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/421", "raw_text": "- **GH-421 · Wave reconciliation is never invoked automatically — wire it post-merge, but fix its ledger write first** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-04 via HQ** — wave_reconcile.py (GH-165) already moves docs, syncs the ledger, regenerates dashboards and replans the next wave, and its CLI is shaped for unattended use; nothing fires it. Measured: #420 and #409 both merged 2026-09-03 and neither reconciled. BLOCKER on ordering — its only ledger call is `releases roadmap sync`, a deliberate no-op in releases-mode, while it still writes shipping into the frozen ROADMAP.md, so automating it first would write a wrong record at machine speed and exit 0. Phase 1 gives it manifest ship / roadmap repoint; Phase 2 wires pull_request:closed; Phase 3 lands the artifacts. — [GH-421-AUTO-WAVE-RECONCILE.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-421-AUTO-WAVE-RECONCILE.md) · [#421](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/421) (rated 85/75/88/50)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 85, "rating_sev": 75, "rating_appeal": 88, "rating_effort": 50, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1N0C5V50EF6E84T906RQE8W", "gh_number": 423, "title": "releases roadmap render: emit the DB as ledger markdown — the missing verb #418 actually depends on", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 45, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-423-ROADMAP-RENDER.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/423", "raw_text": "- **GH-423 · releases roadmap render: emit the DB as ledger markdown — the missing verb GH-418 actually depends on** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-04 via HQ** — QUEUE_PLAN_ROADMAP takes a FILE path and nothing renders roadmap_items in the shape the planner parses, so GH-418 has been summarized with an option (\"accept the shim\") that is empty. The two ledger-bullet parsers already mirror each other by hand, and roadmap_items stores raw_text verbatim, so the verb is a replay not a generator. Leaves the 64KB engine byte-unchanged and serves the nine other skills still reading ROADMAP.md. — [GH-423-ROADMAP-RENDER.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-423-ROADMAP-RENDER.md) · [#423](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/423) (rated 80/60/85/88)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 80, "rating_sev": 60, "rating_appeal": 85, "rating_effort": 88, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1N1Z8Z2150Z58DQJM5PW6PK", "gh_number": 424, "title": "roadmap_items.status_marker has no CLI writer — in releases-mode a row can never leave 🆕", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 46, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-424-ROADMAP-STATUS-MARKER-WRITER.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/424", "raw_text": "- **GH-424 · roadmap_items.status_marker has no CLI writer — in releases-mode a row can never leave 🆕** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-04 via HQ** — roadmap update has --raw-text and --section but no marker arg; repoint writes only doc_path/raw_text; the only thing that ever set it was roadmap sync parsing the legacy markdown, a no-op here. 50 rows sit at 🆕 including shipped work. Ships an enum-validated --status-marker, NOT derivation from raw_text (that re-couples schema to markdown — agy over Codex). Also closes the rollback gap: the journal never snapshots RELEASES.generated.md, so a rewound DB leaves it ahead and releases check fails generation-mismatch after a rollback reported as successful. Hard prerequisite for GH-421. — [GH-424-ROADMAP-STATUS-MARKER-WRITER.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-424-ROADMAP-STATUS-MARKER-WRITER.md) · [#424](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/424) (rated 90/70/75/70)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 90, "rating_sev": 70, "rating_appeal": 75, "rating_effort": 70, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1N1ZJP33J5G3NW3JK6A2YS3", "gh_number": 425, "title": "--gate's provenance check never compares the PR number — it proves TESTS-RESULTS/ is non-empty", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 47, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-425-GATE-PROVENANCE-CHECK.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/425", "raw_text": "- **GH-425 · --gate provenance check never compares the PR number — it proves TESTS-RESULTS/ is non-empty and reports receipts verified** 🆕 **captured 2026-09-04 via HQ** — check_provenance_receipts reads pr_num, walks the tree, trips on the first provenance.jsonl anywhere, never compares it, then prints \"Provenance receipts verified for PR #{pr_num}\". Receipts are committed here, so the gate cannot fail; no test coverage, no red control. The GH-406 defect class inside the flag meant to be the safety catch. Gates closeout, not merging — exposure is a false provenance record. Prerequisite for GH-421 Phase 2. — [GH-425-GATE-PROVENANCE-CHECK.md](PROJECT/2-WORKING/GH-425-GATE-PROVENANCE-CHECK.md) · [#425](https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/425) (rated 78/65/80/85)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 78, "rating_sev": 65, "rating_appeal": 80, "rating_effort": 85, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1S49SPE25SCF9451MANPZ8N", "gh_number": 443, "title": "marathon-triage: verify PRS ratings, then compute, preflight, and dry-run the marathon before it fires", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 50, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-443-MARATHON-RATING-PASS.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/443", "raw_text": "- **GH-443 · marathon-triage: verify PRS ratings, then compute, preflight, and dry-run the marathon before it fires** — rated 60/40/50/55 — [capture](PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-443-MARATHON-RATING-PASS.md)", "status_label_supported": true, "status_label": null, "rating_pri": 60, "rating_sev": 40, "rating_appeal": 50, "rating_effort": 55, "rating_ovr": null, "risk": null}, {"global_id": "rmi-01M1S6GVM9R0EKRND78J9ZV59Q", "gh_number": 445, "title": "runtime:parity — turn shims reject --help when RELAY_AGENT is unset under XYZ_PYTHON=0", "section": "Queue / parked intake", "position": 51, "status_marker": "🆕", "doc_path": "PROJECT/1-INBOX/GH-445-TURN-SHIM-HELP-PARITY.md", "issue_url": "https://github.com/HiQS-Labs/XYZ-forge/issues/445", "raw_text": "- *